{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>From his chosen ones.</b> Some say its meaning is 'from his youth,' and the reason he did not say 'like the words of an elder.' Some attach מבחוריו to 'minister of Moses,' the meaning being that he served him from the day he was a young man. This is not correct, for this event was in the second year. The correct view in my eyes is that מבחוריו means of those chosen to minister to Moses, for others are with him. Know that the word בחור in plural sometimes takes a dagesh and sometimes not, and likewise the word סריס. Perhaps they are two different mishqalim." "<b>כלאם.</b> The lamed is spirantized because of the guttural letter that follows it."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The dagesh reference is to whether the second bet in מבחוריו has a dagesh or not; Ibn Ezra observes variation in plural forms of this pattern."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:20.500133840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}